-- name    : ProEtale_Topology_Comparison_Acyclicity
-- status  : Definition
-- author  : @Idealson
-- created : 2026-11-26T18:33:52.345308+00:00
-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/7fc1e1bc-6ff0-4e0c-aca6-ca4108c02dd4
-- title:
--   Auxiliary lemmas for the acyclicity of pulled-back injective sheaves: affine pro-étale objects, open covers, (bi)product instances
-- statement:
--   This file holds the auxiliary part of the module on acyclicity of pullbacks of injective sheaves. The module's main result, not included here, is that for an injective abelian sheaf $I$ on the small étale site of a scheme $S$, the pullback $\nu^*I$ to the pro-étale site has vanishing higher cohomology on affine pro-étale objects.
--
--   The file contains:
--
--   1. **From pro-étale to affine pro-étale objects.** An object $X$ of the pro-étale site $S_{\mathrm{pro\acute et}}$ whose structure morphism $X \to S$ is pro-affine-étale is regarded as an object of the affine pro-étale site $S_{\mathrm{aff\text{-}pro\acute et}}$. The inclusion back into $S_{\mathrm{pro\acute et}}$ returns $X$ definitionally.
--   2. **Zariski covers are pro-étale covers.** Let $X \in S_{\mathrm{pro\acute et}}$ and $g_i : V_i \to X$ ($i \in \kappa$, a $u$-small type) be morphisms whose underlying scheme maps are open immersions and are jointly surjective, i.e. every point of $X$ lies in the image of some $g_i$. Then the sieve generated by $\{g_i\}$ is a covering sieve of $X$ for the pro-étale topology.
--   3. **Instances** for the category of abelian sheaves on $S_{\mathrm{pro\acute et}}$: coproducts indexed by any $u$-small type, finite biproducts, and biproducts of any finite $u$-small shape. They are registered explicitly because typeclass search does not find them, or finds them very slowly.
--
--   These are used in the proof, via Cartan's criterion and Čech complexes, that $H^i(U, \nu^*I) = 0$ for $i > 0$ and $U$ affine pro-étale, the key step in comparing étale and pro-étale cohomology.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $S$ is a `Scheme.{u}` and the sheaves take values in `Ab.{u+1}`. Main declarations: `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.AffineProEt.ofProEt`, `AffineProEt.toProEt_obj_ofProEt` and `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ProEt.generate_ofArrows_mem_topology`. Pro-affine-étaleness is the predicate `proAffineEtale X.hom`.
-- source:
--   B. Bhatt, P. Scholze, The pro-étale topology for schemes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.1198 (v2, 17 Dec 2014); cited in the code: BS15, proof of Corollary 5.1.6. Lean source: idealson-nexources/proetale (fork of chrisflav/proetale by C. Merten, J. Jiang and contributors, Apache-2.0), commit 2983805, file Proetale/Topology/Comparison/Acyclicity.lean (declarations needed by the transplanted proofs, unused ones removed).

